DDL (Data Definition Language)

:Used to define and modify database structure such as tables and databases. DDL commands are
generally auto-committed.

Example:
CREATE TABLE Students (ID INT, Name VARCHAR(50));
ALTER TABLE Students ADD Email VARCHAR(100);
DROP TABLE Students;

==============================
DQL (Data Query Language)
:Used to retrieve data from a database.

Example:
SELECT * FROM Students;

==================================
DML (Data Manipulation Language)
:Used to insert, update and delete records in tables.

Example:
INSERT INTO Students VALUES (1,'Rahul');
UPDATE Students SET Name='Aman' WHERE ID=1;
DELETE FROM Students WHERE ID=1;

======================================
DCL (Data Control Language)
:Used to control user permissions and access.

Example:
GRANT SELECT ON Students TO User1;
REVOKE SELECT ON Students FROM User1;

=============================================
TCL (Transaction Control Language)
Used to manage transactions and save database changes.
Example:
COMMIT;
ROLLBACK;
SAVEPOINT sp1;

==============================================

SELECT: Extracts data from a database
Example: SELECT * FROM Students;
===========================================
UPDATE: Updates existing data
Example: UPDATE Students SET Name='Riya' WHERE ID=1;

=================================================
DELETE: Deletes rows from a table
Example: DELETE FROM Students WHERE ID=1;

==============================================
INSERT INTO: Inserts new records
Example: INSERT INTO Students VALUES (2,'Riya');

===============================================
CREATE DATABASE: Creates a new database
Example: CREATE DATABASE CollegeDB;

==============================================
CREATE TABLE: Creates a new table
Example: CREATE TABLE Course (CourseID INT);

==============================================
ALTER DATABASE: Modifies database settings
Example: ALTER DATABASE CollegeDB MODIFY NAME = NewCollegeDB;

=================================================
ALTER TABLE: Modifies table structure
Example: ALTER TABLE Course ADD CourseName VARCHAR(50);

===================================================
DROP TABLE: Deletes a table
Example: DROP TABLE Course;

==================================================
CREATE INDEX: Creates an index for faster searching
Example: CREATE INDEX idx_name ON Students(Name);

==============================================
DROP INDEX: Deletes an index
Example: DROP INDEX idx_name;

=============================================
